[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Ruy Lopez"]
[Variation "Ruy Lopez: Berlin Defense, Anderssen Variation"]
[ECO "C65"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "slow-build,quiet-development"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...Nf6"]
[Start "ruy-lopez-setup 3.Bb5"]

3... Nf6 { The Berlin: Black counterattacks e4 instead of asking the bishop a question. } 4. d3 { Guards e4 calmly. 4.O-O allows ...Nxe4 and a famous endgame full of theory; with d3, White simply builds. } 4... Bc5 ( 4... d6 5. O-O { Castles. White plays c3, Re1 and d4 when ready. } ) 5. c3 { Prepares d4, which would hit the bishop on c5, and gives the bishop on b5 a way back to c2. } 5... O-O ( 5... d6 6. O-O ) 6. O-O { Castles before anything else. } 6... d5 ( 6... d6 7. Nbd2 { The knight heads for f1 and g3, as in the Italian. } ) 7. exd5 { Takes, so Black's queen has to come out and can be hit. } 7... Qxd5 8. Bc4 { Hits the queen and gets the bishop to the diagonal towards f7. } 8... Qd8 9. b4 { Gains space on the queenside and asks the bishop on c5 to move. } 9... Bd6 10. Re1 { The game is level. Plan: Nbd2-e4 or a4 and b5 against the knight on c6, and Bg5 to pin the knight on f6. } *
